Here is a recursive JavaScript function that retries a request 3 times before it resolves the promise:

```javascript
function retryRequest(requestFunction, retries = 3) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    if (retries > 0) {
      requestFunction()
        .then(result => {
          resolve(result);
        })
        .catch(error => {
          if (retries === 1) {
            reject(error);
          } else {
            retryRequest(requestFunction, retries - 1)
              .then(result => {
                resolve(result);
              })
              .catch(error => {
                reject(error);
              });
          }
        });
    } else {
      reject(new Error('Max retries exceeded'));
    }
  });
}
```

