Here's a simple MATLAB code to find prime numbers using the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm. This algorithm works by iteratively marking the multiples of each prime number starting from 2.

```matlab
function primes = prime_search(n)
    % Create the sieve
    sieve = true(1, n);
    sieve(1:2) = false;

    % Sieve of Eratosthenes
    for p = 3:sqrt(n)
        if sieve(p)
            sieve((2*p):p:n) = false;
        end
    end

    % Collect the primes
    primes = find(sieve);
end
```

